a might be optimistic  last year bilateral trade with china  jumped 36 percent to a record 147  billion dollars it's set to reach 250  billion dollars soon that's 40 more than  current trade volume between russia and  the eu  currently russia is china's second  biggest oil supplier providing over 15  percent of its imports  the country also covers five percent of  china's demand for natural gas  meanwhile trade and foodstuffs has been  growing fast in 2019 china allowed the  import of soybeans from russia  last year it added beef to the import  list and just last week wheat  china is also a huge buyer of timber  from russia's far east with imports  worth more than four billion dollars  last year  as for trade in the other direction  china sells machinery mobile phones cars  and consumer products to russia with  exports surging by a third last year  china is also russia's largest foreign  investor having issued at least 125  billion dollars worth of loans for  infrastructure projects that are largely  tied to china's belt and road initiative  russia counts on china as its new key  trade partner  but beijing might show some hesitance  wary of trouble with its western  partners should it run afoul of  sanctions  [Music]  the assembly lines are shut down in the  russian city of kaluga  volkswagen polos tiguans and skoda's  rapid  are no longer being produced following  russia's invasion of ukraine  normally 4 000 people would be working  at vw's facilities in kaluga and nizhny  novgorod  it's located  340 kilometers east of moscow  and it's where vw produces skoda branded  cars the volkswagen group has also  ceased all exports to russia last year  subsidiary porsche delivered 6 000 cars  to russia vw blames the current crisis  and uncertainty for the export stop the  move brings vw in line with other car  makers like bmw and mercedes-benz  leading u.s car makers general motors  and ford have also cut off exports to  russia  [Music]  since russia invaded ukraine oil prices  have been surging  leading industrial nations now want to  tap their oil reserves to mitigate the  situation for consumers and companies  the international energy agency wants to  release 60 million barrels of crude oil  reserves  that's about four percent of all  emergency reserves of one and a half  billion barrels  meanwhile western oil companies continue  to scale down their operations in russia  bp the biggest foreign investor in  russia said it's abandoning its 20 stake  in state oil company rosneft at a cost  of up to 25 billion dollars  also oil giant shell now says it's  ending its cooperation with gas prom in  key oil and gas projects italy's annie  is joining shell and bp  traditionally neutral switzerland will  adopt all the sanctions that the eu has  already imposed on russia over its  invasion of ukraine  switzerland has banned five oligarchs  close to russian president vladimir  putin from entering the country  sporting sanctions against russia have  led to a run on german team schalke  soccer jerseys in the city of gales and  kirschen  demand for sure to the club rose after  the second division team dropped russian  state-owned energy giant gazprom as its  main sponsor  the swedish furniture giant ikea is also  suspending its operations in russia and  belarus affecting nearly 15 000  employees 17 stores and three production  sites in response to the war in ukraine  ikea is one of the largest western  employers in russia  home rental company airbnb says it will  offer free temporary housing for up to a  hundred thousand refugees fleeing  ukraine  ceo brian chesky sent letters to leaders  of poland romania germany and hungary  offering help to house the refugees  more than a million ukrainians have  entered the eu  since the russian invasion  [Music]  the closure of russian airspace  following the invasion is set to cause  massive disruption to international air  cargo and traffic  cargo flights and passenger aircraft to  asia have to take different routes  lufthansa cargo says that flights from  central europe to japan korea and china  can take several hours longer and will  carry up to 20 percent less freight this  will make flights and freight more  expensive  shipping is also feeling the  consequences of the war  and the sanctions against russia  the world's largest container shipping  company maersk suspended nearly all  container deliveries to and from russia  there will be exceptions however for  foodstuffs medicine and humanitarian  goods  german manufacturers are worried about  bottlenecks especially in raw materials  and intermediate products and possible  price increases  german car makers have around 50  suppliers in manufacturing sites in  russia and ukraine  it's still too early to predict what  impact exactly the war will have  russia and ukraine are amongst the  largest exporters of wheat accounting  for about one third of global exports  but these exports are now at risk and  this is hitting poor countries in africa  and latin america in particular  they're dependent upon cheap imports  [Music]  the people of war-torn yemen are very  concerned about the situation in ukraine  yemen's wheat reserves are expected to  last only a few more months but many  like here in the capital sana worry  about rising flower prices  the russian war against ukraine will  affect the whole world and not just us  yemen will undoubtedly be affected  we're an importer of wheat and most of  our food supplies come from abroad  lebanon says it has wheat reserves for  just one more month  its largest silos were destroyed in a  massive explosion in beirut's harbor two  years ago the country depends on wheat  imports with nearly 60 percent coming  from ukraine the government is now  looking for alternative sources  we've reached out to a number of  countries including the us india canada  and europe that produce the soft wheat  that's needed for the air bread styles  we produce in lebanon  turkey depends on wheat imports 